  "term": "substantia nigra",
  "definition": "The substantia nigra is a dark-pigmented area in the ventral midbrain, or the group of cells located there. Its cells make dopamine, a neurotransmitter involved in movement-related functions and mood, and its dark color comes from melanin formed as a by-product of dopamine production.",
